//@version=6
// Break-then-pullback strategy (run on a 5m chart). Runs ORB (15-min) FIRST, then IB (1-hour).
//
// PRIORITY / INTERACTION (when both are enabled):
//   - ORB may enter only BEFORE the IB forms (i.e. before 10:30). Its resting limit is cancelled at 10:30 if unfilled.
//   - If ORB never traded by the time the IB forms -> ORB is abandoned for the day, only IB plays.
//   - An OPEN ORB trade keeps the seat: while it runs, the IB order is HELD BACK - either direction, so the two
//     never stack risk in one direction and never hedge each other. The ORB is left alone to reach its own target.
//   - When the ORB closes (target or stop), the IB limit goes in - unless price already traded through the IB
//     entry level while the IB was held, in which case that pullback was missed and the IB is skipped for the day.
//   - Net effect: both setups can play on the same day, but strictly one at a time.
//   - OPTIONAL (checkbox, off by default): "Carry an unfilled ORB past the IB". Normally an ORB limit that never
//     filled is cancelled when the IB forms. Armed, it keeps resting - so a pullback that only arrives after 10:30
//     is still taken - and it gives way the instant the IB breaks its range and arms a setup of its own.
//
// PER SETUP (each range, independently configurable below):
//   1) At the range close: bias = low-before-high (long) / high-before-low (short) AND the range close in the
//      top half (long) / bottom half (short) of the range - that half is the "Bias %" input, 50 by default,
//      so a range closing a tick the wrong side of its own midpoint takes no trade. Loosen or tighten it there.
//   2) The trade ARMS only AFTER the range level BREAKS. Break type is selectable: "Wick (touch)" or "Close beyond".
//   3) A LIMIT rests at the fib pullback: shallow(0-25%)->25% line, deeper(25-50%)->50% line.
//   4) AVERAGE DOWN (optional): shallow setup -> a 2nd unit at the 50% line. Each of the four entries (ORB first,
//      ORB avg-down, IB first, IB avg-down) carries its OWN contract count and its own risk budget, and the R/R
//      tool draws a box per unit - solid for the first entry, dashed for the add.
//   FILTERS: skip double-break days; skip ORB setups whose range is under the "Min ORB range %" of price.
//   Stop: ALWAYS the far side of the range (100%), both classes. Optional breakeven when the level is reclaimed.
//   TP long/short selectable: range level / +10% / +30% / +50% / HOD-LOD. One setup/day per range, EOD flatten.
//
// PROBABILITY TABLE (bottom right) - how often price REACHES each level from a given starting point, walk-forward:
//   - "From FILL" rows: from the entry fill to the EOD flatten, per range-size bucket.
//   - "From 25% PB" / "From 50% PB" rows: from the moment price retraces to that fib. Two different starting
//     points, two different sets of odds - the deeper pullback is further from the targets, so its numbers move.
//     N is the sample; "Reach" is how often the setup pulls back that far in the first place.
//   The chart itself stays clean - no probability labels. The table tints the row you are currently in instead:
//   the size row of the running setup, and the pullback row for the depth price has reached ("> " marks it).
//
// NOTE: a Pine strategy nets all orders into ONE position (no hedging). The hold-back rule above means ORB and IB
//   are never open at the same time, so the netting never merges two different setups' positions.
strategy("Break-then-Pullback (ORB + IB)", overlay = true, pyramiding = 6, max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500,
     initial_capital = 30000, margin_long = 0, margin_short = 0,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, process_orders_on_close = false,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.5, slippage = 1)
// MODE: the "Run as" switch (first group in the settings) turns every order off - "Indicator - drawings &
//   alerts only" - while the ranges, levels, risk/reward boxes, probability table and break alerts keep running
//   on identical rules. Pine fixes strategy vs indicator at compile time, so the file stays a strategy() either
//   way; it simply trades nothing.
//
// NOTE: position sizing has two modes, picked by checkbox - fixed contract counts, or a flat $ risk per entry.
//   Either way size is set PER ENTRY (four of them: ORB first, ORB avg-down, IB first, IB avg-down). There is no
//   daily loss limit: risk is controlled per trade, and the day ends at the flatten.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mode: strategy or indicator
// Pine decides strategy() vs indicator() when the script compiles, so an input cannot change the file's type.
// What this switch does is silence every ORDER. In Indicator mode the ranges, levels, fib lines, risk/reward
// boxes, probability table and break alerts all keep running on identical rules - the chart is byte for byte
// the same - while nothing is bought or sold, so the Strategy Tester stays empty and the equity curve flat.
// The setup state machine runs in both modes, so the boxes you see as an indicator are exactly the trades the
// strategy would have taken.
gMode     = "Mode"
runMode   = input.string("Strategy - place orders", "Run as", options = ["Strategy - place orders", "Indicator - drawings & alerts only"], group = gMode,
     tooltip = "STRATEGY: the full engine - entries, exits, EOD flatten, daily-loss halt and the PickMyTrade webhook. INDICATOR: none of those, so no trades and an empty Strategy Tester, but every level, box, label, table and break alert still works. Use it to run the setup as a manual-trading overlay, or to put it on a chart without an equity curve.")
ordersOn  = runMode == "Strategy - place orders"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strategy toggles (isolate each for backtesting)
gStrat    = "Strategies (toggle to track each separately)"
runORB    = input.bool(true, "Run ORB strategy", group = gStrat, tooltip = "Turn OFF to backtest the IB strategy alone in the Strategy Tester.")
runIB     = input.bool(true, "Run IB strategy",  group = gStrat, tooltip = "Turn OFF to backtest the ORB strategy alone.")
orbCarry  = input.bool(false, "Carry an unfilled ORB past the IB (test idea)", group = gStrat,
     tooltip = "OFF: an ORB limit that has not filled by the time the IB forms is cancelled - the standard rule. ON: that unfilled limit keeps resting, so a pullback that finally arrives after 10:30 still gets taken. It gives way the moment the IB breaks its own range and arms a setup, and otherwise expires at the ORB cutoff or the EOD flatten. Only ever applies to a setup that broke and armed before the IB formed; it does not let the ORB arm late.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Trade-day filters (see which weekday hurts each)
gDayO     = "Trade days - ORB"
orbMon    = input.bool(true, "ORB Monday",    group = gDayO)
orbTue    = input.bool(true, "ORB Tuesday",   group = gDayO)
orbWed    = input.bool(true, "ORB Wednesday", group = gDayO)
orbThu    = input.bool(true, "ORB Thursday",  group = gDayO)
orbFri    = input.bool(true, "ORB Friday",    group = gDayO)
gDayI     = "Trade days - IB"
ibMon     = input.bool(true, "IB Monday",    group = gDayI)
ibTue     = input.bool(true, "IB Tuesday",   group = gDayI)
ibWed     = input.bool(true, "IB Wednesday", group = gDayI)
ibThu     = input.bool(true, "IB Thursday",  group = gDayI)
ibFri     = input.bool(true, "IB Friday",    group = gDayI)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Risk sizing (PER ENTRY)
// TWO ways to size, one active at a time - tick the one you want; each is followed by its own inputs.
// Either way the four entries are sized independently: ORB first, ORB average-down, IB first, IB average-down,
// so the add can be bigger, smaller or the same as the entry it doubles up on.
gRisk       = "Risk sizing"
mFixed      = input.bool(true,  "1) Fixed contract size", group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1 (default). Trade exactly the four contract counts below - no risk maths at all. The R/R tool, the strategy orders and the webhook all use those counts. If both modes are ticked this one wins; if neither is ticked this one is used.")
orbQty1In   = input.float(2, "   ORB contracts - FIRST entry",    minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the first ORB unit (the limit at the fib pullback).")
orbQty2In   = input.float(2, "   ORB contracts - AVG-DOWN entry", minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the ORB average-down unit. Independent of the first entry - larger to scale in, smaller to add only a probe.")
ibQty1In    = input.float(1, "   IB contracts - FIRST entry",     minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the first IB unit.")
ibQty2In    = input.float(1, "   IB contracts - AVG-DOWN entry",  minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the IB average-down unit.")
mDlr        = input.bool(false, "2) Risk $ per trade", group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 2. Ignore the contract counts: size each entry so ITS OWN risk equals that entry's dollar amount below. The stop distance decides the count, so a wide range buys fewer contracts and a tight one more - the dollar risk stays put. Untick mode 1 for this to take effect. If the amount cannot cover a single contract at that stop distance, the setup is skipped rather than traded at a size you did not ask for.")
orbRiskDlr1 = input.float(150, "   ORB $ risk - FIRST entry",     minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 2. Dollars risked on the first ORB entry, entry to stop.")
orbRiskDlr2 = input.float(150, "   ORB $ risk - AVG-DOWN entry",  minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 2. Dollars risked on the ORB average-down unit. Its stop is the same price but its entry is deeper, so the same dollars buy more contracts than the first entry - lower it if you do not want the add to dominate the setup.")
ibRiskDlr1  = input.float(150, "   IB $ risk - FIRST entry",      minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk)
ibRiskDlr2  = input.float(150, "   IB $ risk - AVG-DOWN entry",   minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk)

// One mode only: fixed contracts wins if both are ticked, and is the fallback if neither is.
rmFixed    = mFixed or not mDlr
sizeByRisk = not rmFixed
modeTxt    = rmFixed ? "Sizing: fixed contracts" : "Sizing: risk $ per entry"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- HARDCODED CONFIG (edit values here)
// Session
tz      = "America/New_York"
sess    = "0930-1600"
orbSess = "0930-0945"
ibSess  = "0930-1030"
flatH   = 15
flatM   = 30
// ORB settings
orbLong   = true
orbShort  = true
orbBreak  = "Close beyond"
orbAvg    = true
orbTpL    = "Ext 10%"
orbTpS    = "Ext 30%"
orbBE     = false
orbQty1   = orbQty1In         // contracts on the first ORB entry     (Risk sizing group)
orbQty2   = orbQty2In         // contracts on the ORB avg-down entry  (Risk sizing group)
orbCutH   = 15
orbCutM   = 0
// IB settings
ibLong    = true
ibShort   = true
ibBreak   = "Wick (touch)"
ibAvg     = true
ibTpL     = "Ext 30%"
ibTpS     = "Ext 30%"
ibBE      = false
ibQty1    = ibQty1In          // contracts on the first IB entry      (Risk sizing group)
ibQty2    = ibQty2In          // contracts on the IB avg-down entry   (Risk sizing group)
ibCutH    = 14
ibCutM    = 0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Filters
gFilt     = "Filters"
noDbl     = input.bool(true, "Skip double-break days (both range sides break)", group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "If the side OPPOSITE the setup direction also breaks (long: price trades below the range low; short: above the range high), cancel the pending entry and take no trade that day. Keeps you to clean one-directional break days only.")
orbBias   = input.float(50, "ORB bias: range must close beyond % of the range", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 0.5, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "The direction test has two parts: which extreme printed FIRST, and where the range CLOSED. This is the second part - how far beyond the midpoint the close must be. 50 is the classic rule (top half for a long, bottom half for a short) but it makes a knife edge out of a range that closes on its midpoint: a close a single tick the wrong side kills the setup. Raise it to demand a more decisive close, or drop it a point or two to stop hairline misses throwing a day away.")
ibBias    = input.float(50, "IB bias: range must close beyond % of the range", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 0.5, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "The direction test has two parts: which extreme printed FIRST, and where the range CLOSED. This is the second part - how far beyond the midpoint the close must be. 50 is the classic rule (top half for a long, bottom half for a short) but it makes a knife edge out of a range that closes on its midpoint: a close a single tick the wrong side kills the setup. Raise it to demand a more decisive close, or drop it a point or two to stop hairline misses throwing a day away.")
orbMinRngPct = input.float(0.40, "Min ORB range (% of price, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 0.05, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "Skip ORB setups whose 15-min opening range is smaller than this % of price (range / range-low * 100). The segmentation test showed the smallest-range ORB bucket (<~0.4%) is the only unprofitable segment - 36% win, PF 0.71. IB is NOT filtered. Set 0 to disable. Tune to your own data; the test sample was limited.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Automation (PickMyTrade webhook -> Tradovate)
grpA      = "Automation - PickMyTrade"
autoOn    = input.bool(false, "Enable webhook alerts", group = grpA,
     tooltip = "Create ONE alert with condition 'alert() function calls only' and paste PickMyTrade's webhook URL. Verify the JSON fields match PickMyTrade's template. Alerts fire on the NET position; ORB and IB are never open at the same time, so each alert maps to a single setup. These need the position the strategy engine holds, so they stay silent in Indicator mode - the manual 'Break alerts' below fire in both modes.")
pmtToken  = input.string("", "PickMyTrade token", group = grpA)
pmtAcct   = input.string("", "Tradovate account id", group = grpA)
pmtSym    = input.string("MNQ1!", "Broker symbol", group = grpA)
pmtType   = input.string("market", "Order type", options = ["market", "limit"], group = grpA)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Break alerts (manual trading)
grpBA     = "Break alerts (manual)"
brkAlerts = input.bool(true, "Alert when ORB / IB level breaks", group = grpBA,
     tooltip = "Fires a notification the moment the ORB or IB range breaks, with the direction and the planned entry/stop/target so you can place the trade yourself. Create ONE alert on this strategy with condition 'alert() function calls only'. (Independent of the PickMyTrade automation above.)")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Risk/Reward tool
grpRR     = "Risk / Reward tool"
showRR    = input.bool(true, "Show risk/reward box at the break", group = grpRR)
showRR2   = input.bool(true, "  ... and a second box for the average-down unit", group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "The average-down unit is a trade of its own - its own entry price, its own contract count, its own risk and reward. With this on it gets its own pair of boxes (dashed border, lighter fill) measured from the 50% line to the same stop and target, plus its own $ label. Turn it off to keep only the first entry's box; the add still appears in the first label's setup-total line.")
showFibs  = input.bool(true, "Show fib retracement lines (25/50/75)", group = grpRR, tooltip = "Dotted lines only, no text: the 25/50/75 levels of the range. Which one is the entry is shown by the R/R box.")
showInfo  = input.bool(true, "Show strategy rules panel", group = grpRR)
ptVal     = input.float(2.0, "$ per point per contract", group = grpRR, tooltip = "MNQ=2, NQ=20, MES=5, ES=50.")
keepBox   = input.int(0, "Keep R/R boxes for the last N setups (0 = all)", 0, 250, group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "0 keeps every past setup's boxes and fib lines, so you can scroll back and review the risk/reward of each historical setup. Pine caps a script at 500 boxes and 500 lines: a setup with an average-down unit draws four boxes, so that is the most recent ~125 setups (~166 fib-line sets). Set a small number to keep only the newest setups on the chart.")
keepLab   = input.int(3, "Keep R/R labels for the last N setups (0 = all)", 0, 250, group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "The boxes are cheap to look at; the text labels are what makes a chart unreadable when they stack up. This keeps the $ risk/reward labels on the newest few setups only (both the first entry's and the average-down unit's), while the boxes stay for the whole history. 0 keeps every label.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Historical probabilities
grpP      = "Historical probabilities"
hiLive    = input.bool(true, "Highlight the live setup in the table", group = grpP,
     tooltip = "Tints the table row you are currently in: the range-size row of the setup that is running, and the pullback row for the depth price has reached so far (25% line, then the 50% line). A > marks the row that is live right now, so the odds you are looking at are the ones that apply. Nothing is drawn on the chart.")
showTable = input.bool(true, "Show probability table", group = grpP)
tblPos    = input.string("Bottom right", "Table position", options = ["Top right", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Top left"], group = grpP)
bMode     = input.string("Auto (equal thirds)", "Size buckets", options = ["Auto (equal thirds)", "Manual (%)"], group = grpP,
     tooltip = "Applies to the size-segmented rows only. Range is measured as % of price (range / range-low * 100) so buckets stay comparable as price drifts over time. Auto: split each strategy's own range-% distribution into three equal-count buckets (S/M/L). Manual: use the fixed % thresholds below.")
orbB1     = input.float(0.25, "Manual ORB small/med split (%)", step = 0.05, group = grpP, tooltip = "Used only in Manual mode. ORB range-% below this = Small; between the two = Medium; at/above the med/large split = Large.")
orbB2     = input.float(0.40, "Manual ORB med/large split (%)", step = 0.05, group = grpP)
ibB1      = input.float(0.50, "Manual IB small/med split (%)",  step = 0.05, group = grpP)
ibB2      = input.float(0.80, "Manual IB med/large split (%)",  step = 0.05, group = grpP)
pbSplit   = input.bool(false, "Split the pullback rows by size too", group = grpP,
     tooltip = "OFF (default): one 'after 25% PB' and one 'after 50% PB' row per strategy, pooled across range sizes - the biggest sample, least noise. ON: those rows are repeated per S/M/L bucket (6 rows per strategy); useful once you have a few hundred days, misleading before that.")
autoMode  = bMode == "Auto (equal thirds)"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Shared tracking
inSess     = not na(time(timeframe.period, sess, tz))
newSession = inSess and not inSess[1]
var float dHigh = na
var float dLow  = na
if newSession
    dHigh := high
    dLow  := low
else if inSess
    dHigh := math.max(dHigh, high)
    dLow  := math.min(dLow, low)
tod     = hour(time, tz) * 60 + minute(time, tz)
flatten = tod >= (flatH*60 + flatM)

// day-of-week gates (per strategy)
dow      = dayofweek(time, tz)
orbDayOK = (dow == dayofweek.monday and orbMon) or (dow == dayofweek.tuesday and orbTue) or (dow == dayofweek.wednesday and orbWed) or (dow == dayofweek.thursday and orbThu) or (dow == dayofweek.friday and orbFri)
ibDayOK  = (dow == dayofweek.monday and ibMon)  or (dow == dayofweek.tuesday and ibTue)  or (dow == dayofweek.wednesday and ibWed)  or (dow == dayofweek.thursday and ibThu)  or (dow == dayofweek.friday and ibFri)

or_inR   = not na(time(timeframe.period, orbSess, tz))
or_rDone = not or_inR and or_inR[1]
ib_inR   = not na(time(timeframe.period, ibSess, tz))
ib_rDone = not ib_inR and ib_inR[1]
var bool ibFormed = false
if newSession
    ibFormed := false
if ib_rDone
    ibFormed := true

// position sizer: contracts for a $ budget at a given stop distance (points).
// round: fractional <= .5 -> down, > .5 -> up (2.1-2.5 -> 2, >2.5 -> 3). A budget too small for a single
// contract returns 0, and the ">= 1" guards on the entries below simply skip that setup.
f_size(float budget, float ptDist) =>
    perC = ptDist * ptVal
    raw  = perC > 0 ? budget / perC : 0.0
    fr   = raw - math.floor(raw)
    fr > 0.5 ? math.ceil(raw) : math.floor(raw)

// TP resolver
f_tp(int d, float rH, float rL, float rg, float dHi, float dLo, string tpL, string tpS) =>
    d == 1 ? (tpL == "HOD/LOD" ? dHi : tpL == "Ext 10%" ? rH + 0.10*rg : tpL == "Ext 30%" ? rH + 0.30*rg : tpL == "Ext 50%" ? rH + 0.50*rg : rH) : (tpS == "HOD/LOD" ? dLo : tpS == "Ext 10%" ? rL - 0.10*rg : tpS == "Ext 30%" ? rL - 0.30*rg : tpS == "Ext 50%" ? rL - 0.50*rg : rL)

// ================================================================ Historical-probability stats
// TWO walk-forward studies are collected (a day is only added to the sample after its EOD flatten, so the numbers
// shown on any bar never contain data from that day or later):
//
//   A) FILL -> EOD, segmented by range size. One record per FILLED trade: did price TOUCH each level between the
//      fill and the EOD flatten? Range is stored as % of price (range / range-low * 100) so the S/M/L buckets stay
//      comparable as price drifts over the years. These are the "size" rows of the table.
//
//   B) PULLBACK -> EOD. One record per SETUP THAT BROKE its range (whether or not the order was actually placed -
//      a day where the IB was held back behind an open ORB still tells you what price did). It answers: once price has
//      retraced to the 25% fib, how often does it go on to tag each TP extension? And the same from the 50% fib.
//      On the very bar that reaches the pullback, a level counts only if the CLOSE is already beyond it - the last
//      tick of that bar sits past the level, so it was traded after the retrace. From the next bar on, an ordinary
//      wick touch counts. That keeps the ordering honest without throwing away the entry candle.
//      The 50% line can only be reached through the 25% line, so the 50% sample is a subset of the 25% one.
//      Read a cell as: "of the setups that pulled back this far, X% went on to trade that level (by 15:30 ET)".
//      SL columns use the same conditioning, so a row shows the reward AND the risk that follow the pullback.
f_pct(int hit, int n) => n > 0 ? 100.0 * hit / n : na
f_pctStr(int hit, int n) =>
    p = f_pct(hit, n)
    na(p) ? "-" : str.tostring(p, "#") + "%"

// ---- study A: one record per filled trade -------------------------------------------------------------------
var tRng   = array.new_float(0)
var tStrat = array.new_int(0)
var tSL100 = array.new_int(0)
var tSL75  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP0   = array.new_int(0)
var tTP10  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP30  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP50  = array.new_int(0)

f_pushTrade(int s, float rng, bool s100, bool s75, bool t0, bool t10, bool t30, bool t50) =>
    array.push(tRng,   rng)
    array.push(tStrat, s)
    array.push(tSL100, s100 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tSL75,  s75  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP0,   t0   ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP10,  t10  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP30,  t30  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP50,  t50  ? 1 : 0)

// ranges recorded so far for one strategy (walk-forward: only days finalized before now)
f_ranges(int s) =>
    tmp = array.new_float(0)
    if array.size(tRng) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(tRng) - 1
            if array.get(tStrat, i) == s
                array.push(tmp, array.get(tRng, i))
    tmp

// tercile boundaries for a strategy (na until >=3 samples); in manual mode the caller passes fixed thresholds
f_b1(array<float> rr) => array.size(rr) < 3 ? na : array.percentile_linear_interpolation(rr, 33.33333)
f_b2(array<float> rr) => array.size(rr) < 3 ? na : array.percentile_linear_interpolation(rr, 66.66667)
f_bkt(float rng, float b1, float b2) => (na(b1) or na(b2)) ? 0 : rng < b1 ? 0 : rng < b2 ? 1 : 2

// counts [n, sl100, sl75, tp0, tp10, tp30, tp50] for one strategy+bucket given the boundaries
f_seg(int s, int bkt, float b1, float b2) =>
    nn = 0
    a0 = 0
    a1 = 0
    a2 = 0
    a3 = 0
    a4 = 0
    a5 = 0
    if array.size(tRng) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(tRng) - 1
            if array.get(tStrat, i) == s and f_bkt(array.get(tRng, i), b1, b2) == bkt
                nn := nn + 1
                a0 := a0 + array.get(tSL100, i)
                a1 := a1 + array.get(tSL75,  i)
                a2 := a2 + array.get(tTP0,   i)
                a3 := a3 + array.get(tTP10,  i)
                a4 := a4 + array.get(tTP30,  i)
                a5 := a5 + array.get(tTP50,  i)
    [nn, a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5]

// ---- study B: one record per armed setup, conditioned on how deep the pullback went --------------------------
// Level order used everywhere below: 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100.
var pbStrat = array.new_int(0)
var pbRngP  = array.new_float(0)
var pbR25   = array.new_int(0)      // did price retrace to the 25% fib
var pbR50   = array.new_int(0)      // ... and to the 50% fib
var pb25_0  = array.new_int(0)      // levels reached from the 25% retrace onward
var pb25_1  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_2  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_3  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_4  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_5  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_0  = array.new_int(0)      // levels reached from the 50% retrace onward
var pb50_1  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_2  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_3  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_4  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_5  = array.new_int(0)

f_pbPush(int s, float rngP, bool r25, bool r50, array<bool> h25, array<bool> h50) =>
    array.push(pbStrat, s)
    array.push(pbRngP,  rngP)
    array.push(pbR25,   r25 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pbR50,   r50 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_0, array.get(h25, 0) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_1, array.get(h25, 1) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_2, array.get(h25, 2) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_3, array.get(h25, 3) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_4, array.get(h25, 4) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_5, array.get(h25, 5) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_0, array.get(h50, 0) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_1, array.get(h50, 1) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_2, array.get(h50, 2) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_3, array.get(h50, 3) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_4, array.get(h50, 4) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_5, array.get(h50, 5) ? 1 : 0)

// counts for one strategy at one pullback depth. depth 0 = reached the 25% fib, 1 = reached the 50% fib.
// bkt = -1 pools all range sizes; 0/1/2 restricts to the S/M/L bucket defined by b1/b2.
// Returns [setups armed, setups that reached that pullback, then TP0, TP10, TP30, TP50, SL75, SL100 counts].
f_pbSeg(int s, int depth, int bkt, float b1, float b2) =>
    nAll = 0
    nn   = 0
    h0 = 0
    h1 = 0
    h2 = 0
    h3 = 0
    h4 = 0
    h5 = 0
    if array.size(pbStrat) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pbStrat) - 1
            if array.get(pbStrat, i) == s and (bkt < 0 or f_bkt(array.get(pbRngP, i), b1, b2) == bkt)
                nAll := nAll + 1
                if (depth == 0 ? array.get(pbR25, i) : array.get(pbR50, i)) == 1
                    nn := nn + 1
                    h0 := h0 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_0, i) : array.get(pb50_0, i))
                    h1 := h1 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_1, i) : array.get(pb50_1, i))
                    h2 := h2 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_2, i) : array.get(pb50_2, i))
                    h3 := h3 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_3, i) : array.get(pb50_3, i))
                    h4 := h4 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_4, i) : array.get(pb50_4, i))
                    h5 := h5 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_5, i) : array.get(pb50_5, i))
    [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5]

// ================================================================ ORB ENGINE (runs first)
var float or_rH = na
var float or_rL = na
var int   or_rHbar = na
var int   or_rLbar = na
var int   or_dir = 0
var bool  or_shallow = false
var float or_e1 = na
var float or_e2 = na
var float or_zstop = na
var float or_rng = na
var bool  or_broke = false
var bool  or_placed = false
var bool  or_f1 = false
var bool  or_f2 = false
var float or_avgPx = na
var float or_curStop = na
var float or_curTP = na
var bool  or_beDone = false
var bool  or_closed = false
var bool  or_oppBroke = false
var float orbSz1 = na
var float orbSz2 = na

if newSession
    or_rH := na
    or_rL := na
    or_dir := 0
    or_shallow := false
    or_e1 := na
    or_e2 := na
    or_zstop := na
    or_rng := na
    or_broke := false
    or_placed := false
    or_f1 := false
    or_f2 := false
    or_avgPx := na
    or_curStop := na
    or_curTP := na
    or_beDone := false
    or_closed := false
    or_oppBroke := false
    orbSz1 := na
    orbSz2 := na
if or_inR
    if na(or_rH) or high > or_rH
        or_rH := high
        or_rHbar := bar_index
    if na(or_rL) or low < or_rL
        or_rL := low
        or_rLbar := bar_index
if or_rDone and not na(or_rH) and or_rH > or_rL
    or_rng := or_rH - or_rL
    or_lf = or_rLbar < or_rHbar
    or_pos = (close[1] - or_rL) / or_rng
    orbBiasF = orbBias / 100.0
    if orbLong and or_lf and or_pos >= orbBiasF
        or_dir := 1
        or_shallow := or_pos >= 0.75
        or_e1 := or_shallow ? or_rL + 0.75*or_rng : or_rL + 0.5*or_rng
        or_e2 := or_rL + 0.5*or_rng
        or_zstop := or_rL                     // the stop is ALWAYS the far side of the range
    else if orbShort and (not or_lf) and or_pos <= 1.0 - orbBiasF
        or_dir := -1
        or_shallow := or_pos <= 0.25
        or_e1 := or_shallow ? or_rL + 0.25*or_rng : or_rL + 0.5*or_rng
        or_e2 := or_rL + 0.5*or_rng
        or_zstop := or_rH                     // the stop is ALWAYS the far side of the range
    if or_dir != 0
        // each unit is sized on its own budget and its own stop distance (the add sits closer to the stop)
        orbSz1 := sizeByRisk ? f_size(orbRiskDlr1, math.abs(or_e1 - or_zstop)) : orbQty1
        orbSz2 := sizeByRisk ? f_size(orbRiskDlr2, math.abs(or_e2 - or_zstop)) : orbQty2
or_useAdd = orbAvg and or_shallow and not na(or_e2)
// break by selected type
or_brk = orbBreak == "Wick (touch)" ? ((or_dir == 1 and high >= or_rH) or (or_dir == -1 and low <= or_rL)) : ((or_dir == 1 and close > or_rH) or (or_dir == -1 and close < or_rL))
if or_dir != 0 and or_brk
    or_broke := true
// double-break detection: opposite range extreme is violated
if or_dir == 1 and low < or_rL
    or_oppBroke := true
if or_dir == -1 and high > or_rH
    or_oppBroke := true
// entry window: before IB forms (when IB is on), within ORB cutoff otherwise, on an allowed weekday
orbSizeOK = orbMinRngPct <= 0 or (not na(or_rng) and or_rL > 0 and or_rng / or_rL * 100 >= orbMinRngPct)
orbWin = inSess and orbDayOK and tod <= (orbCutH*60 + orbCutM) and (not runIB or not ibFormed) and orbSizeOK
if runORB and or_dir != 0 and or_broke and not or_placed and not or_closed and orbWin and not flatten and (not noDbl or not or_oppBroke) and orbSz1 >= 1
    if ordersOn
        if or_dir == 1
            strategy.entry("ORL", strategy.long, qty = orbSz1, limit = or_e1)
            if or_useAdd and orbSz2 >= 1
                strategy.entry("ORL2", strategy.long, qty = orbSz2, limit = or_e2)
        else
            strategy.entry("ORS", strategy.short, qty = orbSz1, limit = or_e1)
            if or_useAdd and orbSz2 >= 1
                strategy.entry("ORS2", strategy.short, qty = orbSz2, limit = or_e2)
    or_placed := true                       // the setup is tracked in both modes; only the order is optional
if or_placed and not or_closed
    if or_dir == 1
        if not or_f1 and low <= or_e1
            or_f1 := true
        if or_useAdd and not or_f2 and low <= or_e2
            or_f2 := true
    if or_dir == -1
        if not or_f1 and high >= or_e1
            or_f1 := true
        if or_useAdd and not or_f2 and high >= or_e2
            or_f2 := true
or_firstFill = (or_f1 or or_f2) and not (or_f1[1] or or_f2[1])
if or_f1 or or_f2
    or_avgPx := or_f1 and or_f2 ? (or_e1 + or_e2) / 2 : or_f1 ? or_e1 : or_e2
if or_firstFill
    or_curStop := or_zstop
    or_curTP := f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, orbTpL, orbTpS)
    or_beDone := false
if orbBE and not or_beDone and (or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed
    if or_dir == 1 and high >= or_rH
        or_curStop := math.max(or_curStop, or_avgPx)
        or_beDone := true
    if or_dir == -1 and low <= or_rL
        or_curStop := math.min(or_curStop, or_avgPx)
        or_beDone := true
if ordersOn and not na(or_curStop)
    strategy.exit("ORLx",  from_entry = "ORL",  stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
    strategy.exit("ORL2x", from_entry = "ORL2", stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
    strategy.exit("ORSx",  from_entry = "ORS",  stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
    strategy.exit("ORS2x", from_entry = "ORS2", stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
if (or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed and not na(or_curStop)
    if or_dir == 1 and (low <= or_curStop or high >= or_curTP)
        or_closed := true
    if or_dir == -1 and (high >= or_curStop or low <= or_curTP)
        or_closed := true
// cancel resting ORB entries once the window closes unfilled, or done/flat/off/double-break.
// CARRY: with the option armed, an unfilled ORB limit survives the IB forming. It still dies at the ORB cutoff,
// on a double-break, on the daily halt or at the flatten - and it gives way as soon as the IB arms its own setup,
// which is handled after the IB engine below (ib_broke is not known this early in the bar).
orbHold = orbCarry and or_placed and not (or_f1 or or_f2) and inSess and orbDayOK and tod <= (orbCutH*60 + orbCutM)
if ordersOn and (or_closed or flatten or not runORB or (noDbl and or_oppBroke) or ((not orbWin) and not (or_f1 or or_f2) and not orbHold))
    strategy.cancel("ORL")
    strategy.cancel("ORL2")
    strategy.cancel("ORS")
    strategy.cancel("ORS2")

// ---- ORB study A: from the fill to EOD, did price touch each level? ----
var bool  or_trk    = false
var int   or_tdir   = 0
var float orL_sl100 = na
var float orL_sl75  = na
var float orL_tp0   = na
var float orL_tp10  = na
var float orL_tp30  = na
var float orL_tp50  = na
var bool  orR_sl100 = false
var bool  orR_sl75  = false
var bool  orR_tp0   = false
var bool  orR_tp10  = false
var bool  orR_tp30  = false
var bool  orR_tp50  = false
if newSession
    or_trk := false
if or_firstFill and not na(or_rng)
    or_trk    := true
    or_tdir   := or_dir
    orL_sl100 := or_dir == 1 ? or_rL : or_rH
    orL_sl75  := or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * or_rng
    orL_tp0   := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL
    orL_tp10  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.10*or_rng : or_rL - 0.10*or_rng
    orL_tp30  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.30*or_rng : or_rL - 0.30*or_rng
    orL_tp50  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.50*or_rng : or_rL - 0.50*or_rng
    orR_sl100 := false
    orR_sl75  := false
    orR_tp0   := false
    orR_tp10  := false
    orR_tp30  := false
    orR_tp50  := false
if or_trk
    if or_tdir == 1
        orR_tp0   := orR_tp0   or high >= orL_tp0
        orR_tp10  := orR_tp10  or high >= orL_tp10
        orR_tp30  := orR_tp30  or high >= orL_tp30
        orR_tp50  := orR_tp50  or high >= orL_tp50
        orR_sl75  := orR_sl75  or low  <= orL_sl75
        orR_sl100 := orR_sl100 or low  <= orL_sl100
    else
        orR_tp0   := orR_tp0   or low  <= orL_tp0
        orR_tp10  := orR_tp10  or low  <= orL_tp10
        orR_tp30  := orR_tp30  or low  <= orL_tp30
        orR_tp50  := orR_tp50  or low  <= orL_tp50
        orR_sl75  := orR_sl75  or high >= orL_sl75
        orR_sl100 := orR_sl100 or high >= orL_sl100
    if flatten
        f_pushTrade(0, or_rng / or_rL * 100, orR_sl100, orR_sl75, orR_tp0, orR_tp10, orR_tp30, orR_tp50)
        or_trk := false

// ---- ORB study B: armed -> 25% / 50% pullback -> which levels print from there, filed at the EOD flatten ----
var bool  orP_act  = false
var int   orP_dir  = 0
var float orP_rngP = na
var float orP_p25  = na
var float orP_p50  = na
var bool  orP_r25  = false
var bool  orP_r50  = false
var orP_lv  = array.new_float(6, na)      // 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100
var orP_h25 = array.new_bool(6, false)
var orP_h50 = array.new_bool(6, false)
if newSession
    orP_act := false
if or_broke and not or_broke[1] and or_dir != 0 and not na(or_rng) and or_rL > 0
    orP_act  := true
    orP_dir  := or_dir
    orP_rngP := or_rng / or_rL * 100
    orP_p25  := or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.75 : 0.25) * or_rng
    orP_p50  := or_rL + 0.50 * or_rng
    orP_r25  := false
    orP_r50  := false
    array.set(orP_lv, 0, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL)
    array.set(orP_lv, 1, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.10*or_rng : or_rL - 0.10*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 2, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.30*or_rng : or_rL - 0.30*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 3, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.50*or_rng : or_rL - 0.50*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 4, or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 5, or_dir == 1 ? or_rL : or_rH)
    for k = 0 to 5
        array.set(orP_h25, k, false)
        array.set(orP_h50, k, false)
if orP_act
    up    = orP_dir == 1
    new25 = false
    new50 = false
    if not orP_r25 and (up ? low <= orP_p25 : high >= orP_p25)
        orP_r25 := true
        new25    := true
    if not orP_r50 and (up ? low <= orP_p50 : high >= orP_p50)
        orP_r50 := true
        new50    := true
    // On the bar that REACHES the pullback the touch must be confirmed by the CLOSE: the last tick of that bar is
    // beyond the level, so it traded there after the retrace low/high. Later bars count an ordinary wick touch.
    for k = 0 to 5
        lv   = array.get(orP_lv, k)
        isTp = k <= 3
        wick = isTp ? (up ? high >= lv : low <= lv) : (up ? low <= lv : high >= lv)
        cls  = isTp ? (up ? close >= lv : close <= lv) : (up ? close <= lv : close >= lv)
        if orP_r25 and (new25 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(orP_h25, k, true)
        if orP_r50 and (new50 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(orP_h50, k, true)
    if flatten
        f_pbPush(0, orP_rngP, orP_r25, orP_r50, orP_h25, orP_h50)
        orP_act := false

// ================================================================ IB ENGINE
var float ib_rH = na
var float ib_rL = na
var int   ib_rHbar = na
var int   ib_rLbar = na
var int   ib_dir = 0
var bool  ib_shallow = false
var float ib_e1 = na
var float ib_e2 = na
var float ib_zstop = na
var float ib_rng = na
var bool  ib_broke = false
var bool  ib_placed = false
var bool  ib_f1 = false
var bool  ib_f2 = false
var float ib_avgPx = na
var float ib_curStop = na
var float ib_curTP = na
var bool  ib_beDone = false
var bool  ib_closed = false
var bool  ib_oppBroke = false
var bool  ib_missed = false      // the IB pullback was reached while an ORB trade held the seat -> skip IB today
var float ibSz1 = na
var float ibSz2 = na

if newSession
    ib_rH := na
    ib_rL := na
    ib_dir := 0
    ib_shallow := false
    ib_e1 := na
    ib_e2 := na
    ib_zstop := na
    ib_rng := na
    ib_broke := false
    ib_placed := false
    ib_f1 := false
    ib_f2 := false
    ib_avgPx := na
    ib_curStop := na
    ib_curTP := na
    ib_beDone := false
    ib_closed := false
    ib_oppBroke := false
    ib_missed := false
    ibSz1 := na
    ibSz2 := na
if ib_inR
    if na(ib_rH) or high > ib_rH
        ib_rH := high
        ib_rHbar := bar_index
    if na(ib_rL) or low < ib_rL
        ib_rL := low
        ib_rLbar := bar_index
if ib_rDone and not na(ib_rH) and ib_rH > ib_rL
    ib_rng := ib_rH - ib_rL
    ib_lf = ib_rLbar < ib_rHbar
    ib_pos = (close[1] - ib_rL) / ib_rng
    ibBiasF = ibBias / 100.0
    if ibLong and ib_lf and ib_pos >= ibBiasF
        ib_dir := 1
        ib_shallow := ib_pos >= 0.75
        ib_e1 := ib_shallow ? ib_rL + 0.75*ib_rng : ib_rL + 0.5*ib_rng
        ib_e2 := ib_rL + 0.5*ib_rng
        ib_zstop := ib_rL                     // the stop is ALWAYS the far side of the range
    else if ibShort and (not ib_lf) and ib_pos <= 1.0 - ibBiasF
        ib_dir := -1
        ib_shallow := ib_pos <= 0.25
        ib_e1 := ib_shallow ? ib_rL + 0.25*ib_rng : ib_rL + 0.5*ib_rng
        ib_e2 := ib_rL + 0.5*ib_rng
        ib_zstop := ib_rH                     // the stop is ALWAYS the far side of the range
    if ib_dir != 0
        ibSz1 := sizeByRisk ? f_size(ibRiskDlr1, math.abs(ib_e1 - ib_zstop)) : ibQty1
        ibSz2 := sizeByRisk ? f_size(ibRiskDlr2, math.abs(ib_e2 - ib_zstop)) : ibQty2
// INTERACTION: an OPEN ORB trade always keeps priority - the IB order is held back (either direction, so the two
// can never stack risk or hedge each other). The IB is not cancelled, only delayed: the moment the ORB closes
// (target, stop or the flip of its own exit) the IB limit goes in, provided price has NOT already traded through
// the IB entry level while it was held. If it has, that pullback was missed and the IB is done for the day.
orbLive = runORB and (or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed
ib_useAdd = ibAvg and ib_shallow and not na(ib_e2)
ib_brk = ibBreak == "Wick (touch)" ? ((ib_dir == 1 and high >= ib_rH) or (ib_dir == -1 and low <= ib_rL)) : ((ib_dir == 1 and close > ib_rH) or (ib_dir == -1 and close < ib_rL))
if ib_dir != 0 and ib_brk
    ib_broke := true
if ib_dir == 1 and low < ib_rL
    ib_oppBroke := true
if ib_dir == -1 and high > ib_rH
    ib_oppBroke := true
ibWin = inSess and ibDayOK and tod <= (ibCutH*60 + ibCutM)
// hold the IB while an ORB trade is live; if its entry level trades through during the hold, the IB is forfeited
if runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_placed and not ib_closed and orbLive and not na(ib_e1)
    if (ib_dir == 1 and low <= ib_e1) or (ib_dir == -1 and high >= ib_e1)
        ib_missed := true
if runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_placed and not ib_closed and ibWin and not flatten and (not noDbl or not ib_oppBroke) and ibSz1 >= 1 and not orbLive and not ib_missed
    if ordersOn
        if ib_dir == 1
            strategy.entry("IBL", strategy.long, qty = ibSz1, limit = ib_e1)
            if ib_useAdd and ibSz2 >= 1
                strategy.entry("IBL2", strategy.long, qty = ibSz2, limit = ib_e2)
        else
            strategy.entry("IBS", strategy.short, qty = ibSz1, limit = ib_e1)
            if ib_useAdd and ibSz2 >= 1
                strategy.entry("IBS2", strategy.short, qty = ibSz2, limit = ib_e2)
    ib_placed := true
if ib_placed and not ib_closed
    if ib_dir == 1
        if not ib_f1 and low <= ib_e1
            ib_f1 := true
        if ib_useAdd and not ib_f2 and low <= ib_e2
            ib_f2 := true
    if ib_dir == -1
        if not ib_f1 and high >= ib_e1
            ib_f1 := true
        if ib_useAdd and not ib_f2 and high >= ib_e2
            ib_f2 := true
ib_firstFill = (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not (ib_f1[1] or ib_f2[1])
if ib_f1 or ib_f2
    ib_avgPx := ib_f1 and ib_f2 ? (ib_e1 + ib_e2) / 2 : ib_f1 ? ib_e1 : ib_e2
if ib_firstFill
    ib_curStop := ib_zstop
    ib_curTP := f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ibTpL, ibTpS)
    ib_beDone := false
if ibBE and not ib_beDone and (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ib_closed
    if ib_dir == 1 and high >= ib_rH
        ib_curStop := math.max(ib_curStop, ib_avgPx)
        ib_beDone := true
    if ib_dir == -1 and low <= ib_rL
        ib_curStop := math.min(ib_curStop, ib_avgPx)
        ib_beDone := true
if ordersOn and not na(ib_curStop)
    strategy.exit("IBLx",  from_entry = "IBL",  stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
    strategy.exit("IBL2x", from_entry = "IBL2", stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
    strategy.exit("IBSx",  from_entry = "IBS",  stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
    strategy.exit("IBS2x", from_entry = "IBS2", stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
if (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ib_closed and not na(ib_curStop)
    if ib_dir == 1 and (low <= ib_curStop or high >= ib_curTP)
        ib_closed := true
    if ib_dir == -1 and (high >= ib_curStop or low <= ib_curTP)
        ib_closed := true
if ordersOn and (ib_closed or flatten or not runIB or (noDbl and ib_oppBroke) or ((not ibWin) and not (ib_f1 or ib_f2)))
    strategy.cancel("IBL")
    strategy.cancel("IBL2")
    strategy.cancel("IBS")
    strategy.cancel("IBS2")

// CARRY hand-over: the moment the IB breaks its range and has a valid setup, a carried ORB limit that is still
// unfilled is dropped - the IB gets the seat. A carried ORB that HAS filled keeps it (see orbLive above).
if runORB and orbCarry and not or_closed and not (or_f1 or or_f2) and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke
    if ordersOn
        strategy.cancel("ORL")
        strategy.cancel("ORL2")
        strategy.cancel("ORS")
        strategy.cancel("ORS2")
    or_closed := true

// ---- IB study A: from the fill to EOD, did price touch each level? ----
var bool  ib_trk    = false
var int   ib_tdir   = 0
var float ibL_sl100 = na
var float ibL_sl75  = na
var float ibL_tp0   = na
var float ibL_tp10  = na
var float ibL_tp30  = na
var float ibL_tp50  = na
var bool  ibR_sl100 = false
var bool  ibR_sl75  = false
var bool  ibR_tp0   = false
var bool  ibR_tp10  = false
var bool  ibR_tp30  = false
var bool  ibR_tp50  = false
if newSession
    ib_trk := false
if ib_firstFill and not na(ib_rng)
    ib_trk    := true
    ib_tdir   := ib_dir
    ibL_sl100 := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rL : ib_rH
    ibL_sl75  := ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * ib_rng
    ibL_tp0   := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL
    ibL_tp10  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.10*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.10*ib_rng
    ibL_tp30  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.30*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.30*ib_rng
    ibL_tp50  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.50*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.50*ib_rng
    ibR_sl100 := false
    ibR_sl75  := false
    ibR_tp0   := false
    ibR_tp10  := false
    ibR_tp30  := false
    ibR_tp50  := false
if ib_trk
    if ib_tdir == 1
        ibR_tp0   := ibR_tp0   or high >= ibL_tp0
        ibR_tp10  := ibR_tp10  or high >= ibL_tp10
        ibR_tp30  := ibR_tp30  or high >= ibL_tp30
        ibR_tp50  := ibR_tp50  or high >= ibL_tp50
        ibR_sl75  := ibR_sl75  or low  <= ibL_sl75
        ibR_sl100 := ibR_sl100 or low  <= ibL_sl100
    else
        ibR_tp0   := ibR_tp0   or low  <= ibL_tp0
        ibR_tp10  := ibR_tp10  or low  <= ibL_tp10
        ibR_tp30  := ibR_tp30  or low  <= ibL_tp30
        ibR_tp50  := ibR_tp50  or low  <= ibL_tp50
        ibR_sl75  := ibR_sl75  or high >= ibL_sl75
        ibR_sl100 := ibR_sl100 or high >= ibL_sl100
    if flatten
        f_pushTrade(1, ib_rng / ib_rL * 100, ibR_sl100, ibR_sl75, ibR_tp0, ibR_tp10, ibR_tp30, ibR_tp50)
        ib_trk := false

// ---- IB study B: armed -> 25% / 50% pullback -> which levels print from there, filed at the EOD flatten ----
var bool  ibP_act  = false
var int   ibP_dir  = 0
var float ibP_rngP = na
var float ibP_p25  = na
var float ibP_p50  = na
var bool  ibP_r25  = false
var bool  ibP_r50  = false
var ibP_lv  = array.new_float(6, na)      // 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100
var ibP_h25 = array.new_bool(6, false)
var ibP_h50 = array.new_bool(6, false)
if newSession
    ibP_act := false
if ib_broke and not ib_broke[1] and ib_dir != 0 and not na(ib_rng) and ib_rL > 0
    ibP_act  := true
    ibP_dir  := ib_dir
    ibP_rngP := ib_rng / ib_rL * 100
    ibP_p25  := ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.75 : 0.25) * ib_rng
    ibP_p50  := ib_rL + 0.50 * ib_rng
    ibP_r25  := false
    ibP_r50  := false
    array.set(ibP_lv, 0, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 1, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.10*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.10*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 2, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.30*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.30*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 3, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.50*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.50*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 4, ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 5, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rL : ib_rH)
    for k = 0 to 5
        array.set(ibP_h25, k, false)
        array.set(ibP_h50, k, false)
if ibP_act
    up    = ibP_dir == 1
    new25 = false
    new50 = false
    if not ibP_r25 and (up ? low <= ibP_p25 : high >= ibP_p25)
        ibP_r25 := true
        new25    := true
    if not ibP_r50 and (up ? low <= ibP_p50 : high >= ibP_p50)
        ibP_r50 := true
        new50    := true
    // On the bar that REACHES the pullback the touch must be confirmed by the CLOSE: the last tick of that bar is
    // beyond the level, so it traded there after the retrace low/high. Later bars count an ordinary wick touch.
    for k = 0 to 5
        lv   = array.get(ibP_lv, k)
        isTp = k <= 3
        wick = isTp ? (up ? high >= lv : low <= lv) : (up ? low <= lv : high >= lv)
        cls  = isTp ? (up ? close >= lv : close <= lv) : (up ? close <= lv : close >= lv)
        if ibP_r25 and (new25 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(ibP_h25, k, true)
        if ibP_r50 and (new50 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(ibP_h50, k, true)
    if flatten
        f_pbPush(1, ibP_rngP, ibP_r25, ibP_r50, ibP_h25, ibP_h50)
        ibP_act := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- EOD flatten
if ordersOn and flatten
    strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD flat")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Automation: PickMyTrade webhook JSON (net position)
f_pmt(string act, float q, float slp, float tpp) =>
    '{"token":"' + pmtToken + '","account_id":"' + pmtAcct + '","symbol":"' + pmtSym +
      '","action":"' + act + '","quantity":' + str.tostring(q) +
      ',"order_type":"' + pmtType +
      '","sl":' + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(slp)) +
      ',"tp":' + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(tpp)) + '}'
liveORB  = (or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed
autoStop = liveORB ? or_curStop : ib_curStop
autoTP   = liveORB ? or_curTP  : ib_curTP
autoQty  = math.abs(strategy.position_size)   // actual net contracts (respects % sizing)
buyNow   = strategy.position_size > 0 and (strategy.position_size[1] <= 0 or strategy.position_size > strategy.position_size[1])
sellNow  = strategy.position_size < 0 and (strategy.position_size[1] >= 0 or strategy.position_size < strategy.position_size[1])
closeNow = flatten and strategy.position_size[1] != 0
if autoOn and ordersOn and buyNow
    alert(f_pmt("buy",  autoQty, autoStop, autoTP), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if autoOn and ordersOn and sellNow
    alert(f_pmt("sell", autoQty, autoStop, autoTP), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if autoOn and ordersOn and closeNow
    alert(f_pmt("close", 0, 0.0, 0.0), alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Break alerts (fire once when each range breaks)
if brkAlerts and runORB and or_dir != 0 and or_broke and not or_broke[1]
    orTPa = f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, orbTpL, orbTpS)
    alert("ORB BREAK  " + (or_dir == 1 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
         "  | broke " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL)) +
         "  | pullback entry " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_e1)) +
         "  | stop " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_zstop)) +
         "  | target " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(orTPa)), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if brkAlerts and runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_broke[1]
    ibTPa = f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ibTpL, ibTpS)
    alert("IB BREAK  " + (ib_dir == 1 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
         "  | broke " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL)) +
         "  | pullback entry " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_e1)) +
         "  | stop " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_zstop)) +
         "  | target " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ibTPa)), alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Risk/Reward + fib tool
// Drawn when the ENTRY ORDER IS ACTUALLY PLACED (or_placed / ib_placed), so a break that any filter rejects -
// wrong weekday, range too small, past the cutoff, IB already formed, double-break day, daily loss halt, sizing
// under one contract, or an IB waiting behind an open ORB - draws nothing at all.
// ANCHORING: y is price and x is BAR INDEX, both fixed at creation. The box is one bar wide to begin with and its
// right edge is extended bar by bar while the setup is live, so it always covers real bars - it never projects
// into empty space past the last bar and never stretches across a session gap. Nothing moves when you pan or zoom.
// HISTORY: every valid setup keeps its boxes and fib lines, so you can scroll back and read the risk/reward of
// any past setup at the price levels it actually had. Only the text labels are capped (newest few by default),
// since those are what turn a long history into noise. Both limits are inputs; 0 on either means keep everything.
// TWO UNITS, TWO BOXES: the first entry gets a solid box pair and the average-down unit (when it is armed) gets a
// dashed, lighter pair drawn from the 50% line to the same stop and the same target - so each unit's own risk and
// reward in dollars, at its own contract count, can be read straight off the chart.
var array<box>   dBox = array.new<box>()
var array<line>  dLin = array.new<line>()
var array<label> dLab = array.new<label>()

// A setup draws up to FOUR boxes (first entry + average-down unit, two each) and up to TWO labels, so the
// per-setup limits are multiplied out here - "keep the last N setups" means the same thing either way.
f_trimDraws() =>
    if keepBox > 0
        while array.size(dBox) > keepBox * 4
            box.delete(array.shift(dBox))
        while array.size(dLin) > keepBox * 3
            line.delete(array.shift(dLin))
    if keepLab > 0
        while array.size(dLab) > keepLab * 2
            label.delete(array.shift(dLab))

// Markup for ONE entry unit: a green box from its entry to the target, a red box from its entry to the stop, and
// a label carrying that unit's own contracts / $ risk / $ reward. Both units of a setup share the same stop and
// the same target, so the average-down box is the taller reward / shorter risk of the two.
// q     = contracts on THIS entry (each entry has its own count and its own risk budget).
// ent2/q2 = the OTHER unit, passed only on the first entry so its label can also show the setup total; pass
//           na/0 on the average-down unit itself.
// dashed = draw this unit's boxes with a dashed border and a lighter fill, so the add is told apart at a glance.
f_drawRR(int d, float ent, float zstop, float ptp, float q, color sigCol, string tag, float ent2, float q2, bool dashed) =>
    riskUsd = math.abs(ent - zstop) * ptVal * q
    rewUsd  = math.abs(ptp - ent) * ptVal * q
    risk1   = math.abs(ent - zstop) * ptVal
    rew1    = math.abs(ptp - ent) * ptVal
    rrr = riskUsd > 0 ? rewUsd / riskUsd : na
    gCol = color.new(color.green, dashed ? 89 : 82)
    rCol = color.new(color.red,   dashed ? 89 : 82)
    bw = box.new(bar_index, d == 1 ? ptp : ent, bar_index + 1, d == 1 ? ent : ptp, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = sigCol, border_width = 1, bgcolor = gCol)
    br = box.new(bar_index, d == 1 ? ent : zstop, bar_index + 1, d == 1 ? zstop : ent, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = sigCol, border_width = 1, bgcolor = rCol)
    if dashed
        box.set_border_style(bw, line.style_dashed)
        box.set_border_style(br, line.style_dashed)
    txt = tag + "  " + str.tostring(q, "#.#") + " contract" + (q == 1 ? "" : "s") + " @ " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ent)) +
         "\nRisk $" + str.tostring(riskUsd, "#") + " | Reward $" + str.tostring(rewUsd, "#") + " (" + str.tostring(rrr, "#.##") + "R)" +
         "\n1 contract: Risk $" + str.tostring(risk1, "#") + " | Reward $" + str.tostring(rew1, "#")
    if not na(ent2) and q2 > 0
        totR = riskUsd + math.abs(ent2 - zstop) * ptVal * q2
        totW = rewUsd  + math.abs(ptp - ent2)  * ptVal * q2
        txt := txt + "\n+ avg-down " + str.tostring(q2, "#.#") + " @ " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ent2)) +
             "  ->  setup total Risk $" + str.tostring(totR, "#") + " | Reward $" + str.tostring(totW, "#") +
             " (" + str.tostring(totR > 0 ? totW / totR : na, "#.##") + "R)"
    lb = label.new(bar_index + 1, ent, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.gray, dashed ? 35 : 15), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
    array.push(dBox, bw)
    array.push(dBox, br)
    array.push(dLab, lb)
    [bw, br, lb]

f_drawFibs(float rL, float rg, color sigCol, array<line> dest) =>
    array.clear(dest)
    for i = 1 to 3
        y = rL + i * 0.25 * rg
        ln = line.new(bar_index, y, bar_index + 1, y, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(sigCol, 35), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(dest, ln)
        array.push(dLin, ln)

// stretch one live unit's drawings to the current bar; prices stay exactly where they were set
f_growUnit(box bw, box br, label lb) =>
    if not na(bw)
        box.set_right(bw, bar_index)
        box.set_right(br, bar_index)
        if not na(lb)
            label.set_x(lb, bar_index)

f_growFibs(array<line> fib) =>
    if array.size(fib) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(fib) - 1
            line.set_x2(array.get(fib, i), bar_index)

var box   orbBw  = na
var box   orbBr  = na
var label orbLb  = na
var box   orbBw2 = na            // the average-down unit's own pair of boxes
var box   orbBr2 = na
var label orbLb2 = na
var bool  orbGrow = false
var array<line> orbFib = array.new<line>()
if runORB and or_placed and not or_placed[1] and not na(or_e1) and not na(or_zstop)
    orTP = f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, orbTpL, orbTpS)
    orbBw  := na
    orbBr  := na
    orbLb  := na
    orbBw2 := na
    orbBr2 := na
    orbLb2 := na
    if showFibs
        f_drawFibs(or_rL, or_rng, color.new(color.orange, 0), orbFib)
    if showRR
        orbAdd = or_useAdd and orbSz2 >= 1
        [bw, br, lb] = f_drawRR(or_dir, or_e1, or_zstop, orTP, orbSz1, color.new(color.orange, 0), "ORB entry 1", orbAdd ? or_e2 : na, orbAdd ? orbSz2 : 0, false)
        orbBw := bw
        orbBr := br
        orbLb := lb
        if orbAdd and showRR2
            [bwA, brA, lbA] = f_drawRR(or_dir, or_e2, or_zstop, orTP, orbSz2, color.new(color.orange, 0), "ORB avg-down", float(na), 0.0, true)
            orbBw2 := bwA
            orbBr2 := brA
            orbLb2 := lbA
    orbGrow := true
    f_trimDraws()
if orbGrow
    f_growUnit(orbBw,  orbBr,  orbLb)
    f_growUnit(orbBw2, orbBr2, orbLb2)
    f_growFibs(orbFib)
    if or_closed or flatten or (not (or_f1 or or_f2) and not orbWin)
        orbGrow := false

var box   ibBw  = na
var box   ibBr  = na
var label ibLb  = na
var box   ibBw2 = na             // the average-down unit's own pair of boxes
var box   ibBr2 = na
var label ibLb2 = na
var bool  ibGrow = false
var array<line> ibFib = array.new<line>()
if runIB and ib_placed and not ib_placed[1] and not na(ib_e1) and not na(ib_zstop)
    ibTP = f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ibTpL, ibTpS)
    ibBw  := na
    ibBr  := na
    ibLb  := na
    ibBw2 := na
    ibBr2 := na
    ibLb2 := na
    if showFibs
        f_drawFibs(ib_rL, ib_rng, color.new(color.teal, 0), ibFib)
    if showRR
        ibAdd = ib_useAdd and ibSz2 >= 1
        [bw2, br2, lb2] = f_drawRR(ib_dir, ib_e1, ib_zstop, ibTP, ibSz1, color.new(color.teal, 0), "IB entry 1", ibAdd ? ib_e2 : na, ibAdd ? ibSz2 : 0, false)
        ibBw := bw2
        ibBr := br2
        ibLb := lb2
        if ibAdd and showRR2
            [bwB, brB, lbB] = f_drawRR(ib_dir, ib_e2, ib_zstop, ibTP, ibSz2, color.new(color.teal, 0), "IB avg-down", float(na), 0.0, true)
            ibBw2 := bwB
            ibBr2 := brB
            ibLb2 := lbB
    ibGrow := true
    f_trimDraws()
if ibGrow
    f_growUnit(ibBw,  ibBr,  ibLb)
    f_growUnit(ibBw2, ibBr2, ibLb2)
    f_growFibs(ibFib)
    if ib_closed or flatten or (not (ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ibWin)
        ibGrow := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strategy rules panel (top-right)
var table info = na
if showInfo and barstate.islast
    info := table.new(position.top_right, 1, 15, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 50), border_width = 1)
    table.cell(info, 0, 0,  (ordersOn ? "" : "[INDICATOR - no orders]  ") + "BREAK-THEN-PULLBACK  (ORB + IB)",
         text_color = ordersOn ? color.aqua : color.orange, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 1,  "Ranges: ORB 09:30-09:45 | IB 09:30-10:30 (ET)",      text_color = color.white,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 2,  "Direction: low-first = LONG, high-first = SHORT",     text_color = color.white,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 3,  "  + close beyond " + str.tostring(orbBias, "#.#") + "% (ORB) / " + str.tostring(ibBias, "#.#") + "% (IB) of the range",
         text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 4,  "Enter AFTER the range breaks; limit at fib pullback:", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 5,  "  shallow -> 25% line | deeper -> 50% line",          text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 6,  "Stop: always the range extreme (100%)",               text_color = color.white,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 7,  "Target: ORB L +10% / S +30% ; IB +30% extension",    text_color = color.white,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 8,  "Avg-down: 2nd unit @ 50% - own size & risk",          text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 9,  "One at a time: IB waits for an open ORB to close",    text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 13, orbCarry ? "ORB carry ON: unfilled ORB rests past 10:30" : "ORB carry off (unfilled ORB dies at 10:30)", text_color = orbCarry ? color.orange : color.gray, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 10, "Skip double-break days | Flatten 15:30 ET",           text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 11, "Toggle Run ORB/IB + weekdays to isolate results",     text_color = color.aqua,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 12, "Odds live in the table; > marks where price is now",  text_color = color.aqua,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 14, modeTxt + (rmFixed ? "" : " (per entry, fixed capital)"), text_color = color.yellow, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Probability table
// Columns: N = sample size, Reach = how often that starting point is even reached, then the odds of price trading
// to each level from that starting point, before the 15:30 flatten.
//   "From FILL" rows     : start = the entry fill, split by range size. Reach is n/a (the trade filled by definition).
//   "From 25% PB" rows   : start = the moment price retraces to the 25% fib. Reach = share of armed setups that
//                          pull back that far. This is the number to read when your limit at the 25% line fills.
//   "From 50% PB" rows   : same from the 50% fib - a deeper pullback, a different (usually lower) set of odds, and
//                          a smaller sample since price must pass the 25% line to get there.
tPos  = tblPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right : tblPos == "Bottom left" ? position.bottom_left : tblPos == "Top left" ? position.top_left : position.bottom_right
tRows = 8 + (pbSplit ? 12 : 4)

var table probTbl = na

f_tblRow(int row, string lbl, int nn, string reach, int t0, int t1, int t2, int t3, int q75, int q100, color txt, color bg) =>
    table.cell(probTbl, 0, row, lbl,                text_color = txt,          bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(probTbl, 1, row, str.tostring(nn),   text_color = color.white,  bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 2, row, reach,              text_color = color.silver, bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 3, row, f_pctStr(t0,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 4, row, f_pctStr(t1,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 5, row, f_pctStr(t2,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 6, row, f_pctStr(t3,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 7, row, f_pctStr(q75, nn),  text_color = color.red,    bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 8, row, f_pctStr(q100, nn), text_color = color.red,    bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)

// where we are right now, used to tint the row that applies (nothing is drawn on the chart)
cNow = color.new(color.blue, 40)      // the row that is live on this bar
cWas = color.new(color.blue, 78)      // a depth price has already passed through
cOff = color.black

if showTable and barstate.islast
    if na(probTbl)
        probTbl := table.new(tPos, 9, tRows, bgcolor = color.black, border_color = color.new(color.white, 70), border_width = 1, frame_color = color.white, frame_width = 1)
    // live state per strategy: 0 = not in play, 1 = broke, 2 = at the 25% pullback, 3 = at the 50% pullback
    stA  = array.from(orP_act ? (orP_r50 ? 3 : orP_r25 ? 2 : 1) : 0, ibP_act ? (ibP_r50 ? 3 : ibP_r25 ? 2 : 1) : 0)
    rgA  = array.from(orP_act ? orP_rngP : na, ibP_act ? ibP_rngP : na)
    filA = array.from(((or_f1 or or_f2) and not or_closed) ? 1 : 0, ((ib_f1 or ib_f2) and not ib_closed) ? 1 : 0)
    hdr  = array.from("From FILL - by range size", "N", "Reach", "TP0", "TP10", "TP30", "TP50", "75% line", "STOP")
    for c = 0 to 8
        table.cell(probTbl, c, 0, array.get(hdr, c), text_color = color.black, bgcolor = color.white, text_size = size.normal, text_halign = c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_center)
    // ---- section 1: from the fill, segmented by range size ----
    for s = 0 to 1
        rr = f_ranges(s)
        b1 = autoMode ? f_b1(rr) : (s == 0 ? orbB1 : ibB1)
        b2 = autoMode ? f_b2(rr) : (s == 0 ? orbB2 : ibB2)
        nm = s == 0 ? "ORB" : "IB"
        s1 = na(b1) ? "?" : str.tostring(b1, "#.##") + "%"
        s2 = na(b2) ? "?" : str.tostring(b2, "#.##") + "%"
        for bkt = 0 to 2
            [nn, a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5] = f_seg(s, bkt, b1, b2)
            here = hiLive and array.get(stA, s) > 0 and not na(array.get(rgA, s)) and f_bkt(array.get(rgA, s), b1, b2) == bkt
            inTr = here and array.get(filA, s) == 1
            lbl  = (inTr ? "> " : "") + (bkt == 0 ? nm + " S <" + s1 : bkt == 1 ? nm + " M " + s1 + "-" + s2 : nm + " L >=" + s2)
            f_tblRow(s * 3 + bkt + 1, lbl, nn, "-", a2, a3, a4, a5, a1, a0, color.white, inTr ? cNow : here ? cWas : cOff)
    // ---- section 2: from the 25% / 50% pullback ----
    hdr2 = array.from("From PULLBACK", "N", "Reach", "TP0", "TP10", "TP30", "TP50", "75% line", "STOP")
    for c = 0 to 8
        table.cell(probTbl, c, 7, array.get(hdr2, c), text_color = color.black, bgcolor = color.new(color.aqua, 20), text_size = size.normal, text_halign = c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_center)
    for s = 0 to 1
        rr2 = f_ranges(s)
        c1  = autoMode ? f_b1(rr2) : (s == 0 ? orbB1 : ibB1)
        c2  = autoMode ? f_b2(rr2) : (s == 0 ? orbB2 : ibB2)
        nm2 = s == 0 ? "ORB" : "IB"
        st  = array.get(stA, s)
        for d = 0 to 1
            // the deepest pullback price has reached is "now"; a shallower one it already passed is tinted faintly
            depthOn = hiLive and (d == 0 ? st >= 2 : st >= 3)
            isNow   = hiLive and (d == 0 ? st == 2 : st == 3)
            if pbSplit
                for bkt = 0 to 2
                    [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5] = f_pbSeg(s, d, bkt, c1, c2)
                    same = depthOn and not na(array.get(rgA, s)) and f_bkt(array.get(rgA, s), c1, c2) == bkt
                    szn  = bkt == 0 ? "S" : bkt == 1 ? "M" : "L"
                    lbl  = ((same and isNow) ? "> " : "") + nm2 + " " + szn + " from " + (d == 0 ? "25%" : "50%") + " PB"
                    f_tblRow(8 + s * 6 + bkt * 2 + d, lbl, nn, f_pctStr(nn, nAll), h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, d == 0 ? color.aqua : color.yellow, (same and isNow) ? cNow : same ? cWas : cOff)
            else
                [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5] = f_pbSeg(s, d, -1, c1, c2)
                lbl = (isNow ? "> " : "") + nm2 + " from " + (d == 0 ? "25%" : "50%") + " pullback"
                f_tblRow(8 + s * 2 + d, lbl, nn, f_pctStr(nn, nAll), h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, d == 0 ? color.aqua : color.yellow, isNow ? cNow : depthOn ? cWas : cOff)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Visuals
plot(runORB and not na(or_rH) ? or_rH : na, "ORB High", color = color.new(color.orange, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runORB and not na(or_rL) ? or_rL : na, "ORB Low",  color = color.new(color.orange, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runORB and or_dir != 0 and not na(or_e1) ? or_e1 : na, "ORB Entry", color = color.new(color.yellow, 0), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and not na(ib_rH) ? ib_rH : na, "IB High", color = color.new(color.teal, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and not na(ib_rL) ? ib_rL : na, "IB Low",  color = color.new(color.teal, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and ib_dir != 0 and not na(ib_e1) ? ib_e1 : na, "IB Entry", color = color.new(color.aqua, 0), style = plot.style_linebr)
